# 6. Component Design Rules

Every component must have:

* Single responsibility
* Typed props
* Reusability
* Accessibility
* Responsive behavior
* Loading state (if applicable)
* Error handling (if applicable)

No component should exceed 300 lines.

Extract logic into hooks when complexity grows.

---

# 7. UI Primitive Library

Create reusable primitives:

Button

Input

Textarea

Badge

Card

Section

Heading

Container

IconButton

Modal

Dialog

Tooltip

Accordion

Tabs

Chip

Avatar

Spinner

Skeleton

Divider

Tag

Toast

ProgressBar

Every higher-level component must compose these primitives.

---

# 8. Content Strategy

Never hardcode business text inside components.

Store all content in dedicated files.

Example:

hero.ts

services.ts

pricing.ts

faq.ts

testimonials.ts

Changing content should never require editing JSX.

---

# 9. Configuration Strategy

All configurable values belong in config/.

Examples:

Business Name

Phone

Email

Address

Social Links

WhatsApp Number

Pricing

Navigation

SEO

Theme

This enables rapid reuse for future client projects.

---

# 10. State Management

Use local state by default.

React Context only for:

Theme

Global UI

Modal

Navigation

Avoid Redux or Zustand for this project.

Keep the architecture lightweight.

